#: ../../../file_formats.rst:182
msgid "Changing a Format"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats.rst:184
msgid ""
"A change to what Spack writes in one of these formats may require a new "
"version of that format, and of the formats that depend on it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats.rst:186
msgid "**When a new version is required**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats.rst:187
msgid ""
"A new version of a format is required whenever an older version of Spack "
"would misinterpret the file:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats.rst:189
msgid "the meaning of an existing key changes,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats.rst:190
msgid ""
"a new key affects the identity of a spec, for instance because it is part of "
"the DAG hash, or"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats.rst:191
msgid ""
"an older version of Spack would reconstruct a different spec from the same "
"data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats.rst:193
msgid ""
"An optional key that older versions of Spack can safely ignore does not "
"require a new version. For example, the ``spack`` and ``include_concrete`` "
"sections of lockfiles were added in this way (`#32801 <https://github.com/"
"spack/spack/pull/32801>`_, `#33768 <https://github.com/spack/spack/pull/"
"33768>`_)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats.rst:196
msgid "**Which formats are incremented with it**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats.rst:197
msgid ""
"A new version of the spec file requires a new version of the Database and of "
"the lockfile in the same change, as explained in :ref:`file-formats-"
"coupling`. The build cache media types of spec files and indexes include "
"these versions, so they change with them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats.rst:199
msgid ""
"A new version of the Database does not affect the other formats. It requires "
"a decision on whether an index in the previous version can still be read in "
"place, which also applies to upstreams and to the indexes of build caches."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats.rst:201
msgid ""
"A new version of the lockfile does not affect the other formats. A key added "
"by the new version needs a default value for lockfiles in older versions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../file_formats.rst:203
msgid ""
"A new version of the build cache layout does not affect the other formats. "
"The previous version of the layout remains readable, and Spack provides a "
"command to convert a build cache to the new one."
msgstr ""

